1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Most people use AI, machine learning, and deep learning as buzzwords interchangeably. But mathematically, they represent three concentric circles nested like Russian nesting dolls.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Artificial intelligence started in the nineteen fifties with symbolic logic and expert systems. If you write ten thousand if-else statements for chess, you have built AI, but you have zero machine learning.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Traditional machine learning required human engineers to spend months crafting features by hand. Deep learning obliterated that bottleneck by learning hierarchical representations directly from raw pixels and text.

4
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Remember this rule of thumb: When someone says AI today, they usually mean Deep Learning. Tomorrow in Day three, we uncover how computers actually learn functions. Follow NeuBench for the complete ninety-day journey.
